{
  "run_id": "fb98cf677a",
  "final_message": "**Status:** Reproduced\n\n**Expected:** `<template #_duration>` content replaces the fallback of `<slot name=\"_duration\">` in `SubComponent`, as in 3.5.13.\n\n**Actual:** The fallback content is rendered instead. In the reporter's exact SFCs (`<script setup>`, compiled with compiler-sfc), `title` works but `_duration` shows the red default content. The fallback also shows when the slot name is `_slot2`, as in the report's 3.5.13 link.\n\n**Trigger:** `SubComponent` is rendered inside the default slot of a parent whose slots are dynamic, for example a sibling `<template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname>`.\n- The slot name must start with `_`. A name like `d` works.\n- `cond` can be false and the slot doesn't need to exist in `BaseLayout`. A dynamic slot name (`#[x]`) triggers it too.\n- With no dynamic sibling slot, or with the dynamic slot on `SubComponent` itself, it works.\n- The compiled output is the same either way (`_duration: _withCtx(...)` inside `SubComponent`'s slots object). The difference is at runtime.\n\n**Likely cause (not verified):** `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` skips every key starting with `_` when `optimized` is false, which is the case for content rendered through a dynamic-slot `renderSlot` fragment. That drops the user slot `_duration` along with the compiler flag `_`.\n\n**Run:** `npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts` (from the repo root). It exits 1 now, with `<div><p>cond</p><i>FALLBACK</i></div>` instead of `<div><p>cond</p><b>PROVIDED</b></div>`.\n\n**Passes when:**\n- Published `vue@3.5.13` gives `<div><p>cond</p><b>PROVIDED</b></div>` for the same component setup (standalone jsdom script). `vue@3.5.14` and `vue@3.5.17` give the fallback.\n- A throwaway one-line edit to `assignSlots` (restore `_`, `__`, `$stable` and `_ctx` as the only skipped keys) made the check pass with exit 0. I reverted it, so no production code is changed.\n\n**Reliability:** Deterministic.\n\n**Artifacts:** `/work/runs/fb98cf677a/repo/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts` (the check, a new file). The run command is saved in `/work/runs/fb98cf677a/out/run_command.txt`.\n",
  "run_command": "npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..56ab1bb\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@\n+import { createApp, defineComponent } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reported in vuejs/core as: \"Slot <template> not working when its name starts\n+// with an underscore (_) since v3.5.14\".\n+//\n+// Expected: `<template #_duration>` content replaces the `<slot name=\"_duration\">`\n+// fallback in SubComponent, as it did in 3.5.13.\n+// Trigger: SubComponent is rendered inside the default slot of a parent\n+// (BaseLayout) whose slots are dynamic (here: a `v-if` slot `<template>`).\n+test('slot <template> named with a leading underscore replaces the fallback content', () => {\n+  const BaseLayout = defineComponent({\n+    template: `<div><slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot><slot></slot></div>`,\n+  })\n+  const SubComponent = defineComponent({\n+    template: `<slot name=\"_duration\"><i>FALLBACK</i></slot>`,\n+  })\n+  const App = defineComponent({\n+    components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+    data: () => ({ cond: true }),\n+    template: `\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>cond</p></template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #_duration><b>PROVIDED</b></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>`,\n+  })\n+\n+  const root = document.createElement('div')\n+  createApp(App).mount(root)\n+\n+  expect(root.innerHTML).toBe('<div><p>cond</p><b>PROVIDED</b></div>')\n+})\n"
}
